# Config-path resolution baseline (#2888) - captured 2026-08-13.
#
# One entry per "<repo-relative file>|<config path literal>" that is named by a type OUTSIDE
# BotNexus.Gateway.Configuration and that IConfigPathResolver cannot resolve against PlatformConfig.
#
# THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Route the consumer through the path the binder actually reads and
# delete its line, then lower ExpectedBaselineCount in
# ConfigPathResolutionFenceArchitectureTests to match. Never add an entry to silence a new
# violation - that is precisely the drift this fence exists to stop, and Baseline_DoesNotGrow
# will fail if you try. An entry that no longer corresponds to a live violation is also a
# failure (Baseline_ContainsNoStaleEntries), so the file cannot rot into a permanent allow-list.
#
# The file is intentionally empty of entries: at capture time every config-path literal outside
# the configuration project resolved. The mechanism ships anyway, because the alternative is
# inventing it under time pressure the first time a genuine exception appears.
